<p>A traffic problem that's specifically about <strong>organic search</strong> — rankings that won't move, a site Google seems reluctant to crawl, content that never gets found — doesn't need a full website audit covering security headers and colour contrast. It needs an <strong>SEO audit service</strong>: a focused review of the handful of things that actually move rankings, done properly.</p>

<p>That's what this service is. No 72-point checklist padded with items that don't apply to you. Just technical SEO, on-page optimisation, content, and backlink health — reviewed by someone who has done this for hundreds of sites, with a fix list ranked by what will actually move the needle first.</p>

<h2 id="seo-audit-vs-website-audit">SEO Audit vs Website Audit</h2>

<p>These two terms get used interchangeably online, but they shouldn't be. Knowing the difference gets you the right scope instead of paying for checks that don't apply to your problem.</p>

