<h2 id="whats-included">What's Included</h2>

<p>Full Site and Full Site + Competitor Benchmark engagements cover four dimensions in depth. Single Page audits apply the technical and on-page dimensions to the one page in scope. Nothing here is templated — every finding is tied to your actual site.</p>

<p><strong>Technical SEO</strong> — a full-site crawl at the Full Site tier, or a page-level technical check at Single Page. Covers indexation status against Google Search Console, sitemap accuracy, redirect chains, canonical implementation, crawl budget, and JavaScript rendering issues. This is where we find out why Google isn't finding or indexing your pages.</p>

<p><strong>On-page SEO</strong> — title tags, meta descriptions, heading structure, internal linking, keyword-to-content match, and structured data, checked page by page against actual search intent, not against a generic template.</p>

<p><strong>Content</strong> (Full Site engagements) — thin or duplicate content, topical gaps against competitors who outrank you, and which existing pages have the most upside if strengthened rather than replaced.</p>

<p><strong>Backlink profile</strong> (Full Site engagements) — a link-authority overview flagging any toxic links worth disavowing and the realistic link-building opportunities available to you. Benchmarking against your named competitors is included at the Full Site + Competitor Benchmark tier.</p>

<blockquote>Most SEO audits we're asked to review after the fact have the same problem: they list forty issues with no sense of which three actually matter. Ours ranks every finding by expected impact before it reaches you.</blockquote>

<h2 id="who-this-is-for">Who This Is For</h2>

<p><strong>Businesses with a specific ranking problem</strong> — a traffic drop, a stalled site that never broke through, or a migration that hurt rankings. You want a diagnosis and a fix list, not a general check-up.</p>

<p><strong>SEO agencies</strong> needing a second opinion or overflow capacity. Delivered white-label with no AuditWeb branding — resell it as your own work. See our <a href="/website-audit-tools/white-label/">white-label audit tools</a> comparison if you're weighing build-vs-buy for this.</p>

<p><strong>In-house marketers</strong> who want an external technical-SEO specialist to validate priorities before committing developer time to a fix list nobody's confident in.</p>

