<h2 id="how-we-work">How We Work</h2>

<p>You grant read-only access to Google Search Console (Google Analytics optional but useful). We crawl the site and pull 16 months of Search Console history. Competitor Benchmark engagements additionally compare your findings against competitors you name. A senior analyst — not an automated tool alone — reviews every finding and writes the fix list. Full Site audits are delivered within 5 business days. A walkthrough call is included.</p>

<h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>

<h3>What is an SEO audit service?</h3>
<p>A focused review of the factors that affect your organic search rankings and traffic — technical SEO, on-page optimisation, content quality, and backlink profile. It does not cover security or broader performance and UX. See our <a href="/website-audit-services/">full website audit service</a> for that scope.</p>

<h3>How much does an SEO audit service cost?</h3>
<p>From $197 for a single-page or narrow-scope audit up to $897 for a full-site audit with competitor benchmarking. Enterprise and multi-site engagements are quoted individually.</p>

<h3>Do you offer white-label SEO audit services for agencies?</h3>
<p>Yes. Agencies can resell this service under their own brand with no AuditWeb branding on the report. Volume pricing is available for agencies running audits across multiple client accounts.</p>

<h3>How is this different from your free scanner?</h3>
<p>Our <a href="/free-website-audit/">free scanner</a> runs automated checks in 60 seconds and is a good first step. This service adds senior human analysis and a prioritised, written fix list — the difference between a warning list and a strategy.</p>

